  "notes": "{大人|おとな}しい means quiet, gentle, or well-behaved.\n\nKANJI NOTE:\nDespite the kanji {大人|おとな} (adult), this word means 'gentle/quiet', not 'adult-like'. Often written in hiragana.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {静|しず}か: quiet (of places/sounds)\n- {穏|おだ}やか: calm, mild (personality)\n- {従順|じゅうじゅん}: obedient (formal)\n\nPATTERNS:\n- おとなしくする: to behave, be quiet\n- おとなしい{性格|せいかく}: gentle personality\n- おとなしい{色|いろ}: subdued color\n\nNUANCE:\nGenerally positive, but can imply being too passive or lacking assertiveness depending on context.",
